<title>USA: Rubin repeats backing for strong U.S. dollar.</title>
<headline>Rubin repeats backing for strong U.S. dollar.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-11-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Treasury Secretary Robert Rubin Friday reiterated his support for a strong dollar.</p>
<p>&quot;We believe in a strong dollar,&quot; Rubin quipped to reporters to a news conference on the latest economic statistics.</p>
<p>Rubin also said he believed that despite recent depreciation, the Mexican peso had done well when the impact of inflation was taken into account.</p>
<p>Rubin noted the peso had depreciated somewhat, but added &quot;on an inflation adjusted basis the peso has done quite well.&quot;</p>
</text>
